    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d680">

                <pb facs="0745" n="431" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg431"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 611.419/107</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-12-28T18:00:00+00:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">December 28, 1914, 6 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>1351. Your 838, December 26 [24?], and 839, December 26, and [819], December
                        23.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d680-f1"/> I have presented same, but I have little
                    hope of success till an answer is received to the proposed working arrangement
                    which the British Government means to cover this and other difficulties caused
                    by embargo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
